 this notebook.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"!pip uninstall fitz -y\n!pip install pymupdf --quiet\n\n!pip install pytesseract pillow\n!apt-get install -y tesseract-ocr --quiet\n\nimport pytesseract\nfrom PIL import Image\nimport fitz\n\ndef clean_text(text):\n    import re\n    text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text)\n    return text.strip()\n\ndef extract_with_ocr(pdf_path):\n    doc = fitz.open(pdf_path)\n    sentences = []\n    \n    for page_num, page in enumerate(doc):\n        \n        pix = page.get_pixmap(dpi=300)\n        img = Image.frombytes(\"RGB\", [pix.width, pix.height], pix.samples)\n        \n        text = pytesseract.image_to_string(img)\n        text = clean_text(text)\n        \n        spacy_doc = nlp(text)\n        for sent in spacy_doc.sents:\n            clean = sent.text.strip()\n            if clean:\n                sentences.append({\"page\": page_num + 1, \"text\": clean})\n    \n    return sentences\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:53:35.927646Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:53:35.928074Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:53:50.068659Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:53:35.928043Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:53:50.068034Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"\u001b[33mWARNING: Skipping fitz as it is not installed.\u001b[0m\u001b[33m\n\u001b[2K   \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m25.0/25.0 MB\u001b[0m \u001b[31m64.3 MB/s\u001b[0m eta \u001b[36m0:00:00\u001b[0m:00:01\u001b[0m00:01\u001b[0m\n\u001b[?25hRequirement already satisfied: pytesseract in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (0.3.13)\nRequirement already satisfied: pillow in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (11.3.0)\nRequirement already satisfied: packaging>=21.3 in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from pytesseract) (26.2)\nReading package lists...\nBuilding dependency tree...\nReading state information...\ntesseract-ocr is already the newest version (4.1.1-2.1build1).\n0 upgraded, 0 newly installed, 0 to remove and 141 not upgraded.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"cell_type":"code","source":"nlp = spacy.load(\"en_core_web_sm\")\n\nsentences = extract_with_ocr(\"/kaggle/input/datasets/nahuelfuentes/textbook-example/textbook-chapter-1.pdf\")\n\nprint(f\"Total sentence:{len(sentences)}\")\nprint(sentences[0])","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:53:50.06993Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:53:50.070536Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.203869Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:53:50.070505Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.203164Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Total sentence:650\n{'page': 1, 'text': 'DIGITAL SYSTEMS AND INFORMATION for computations with discrete numeric elements called digits (the Latin word for fingers)—hence the term digital computer.'}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Extraction","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Concepts","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"First we need to capture the concepts in the textbooks, we can't use plain **SpaCy** for this because the *EN* captures proper nouns such as people or places, but can't capture concepts that are plain nouns. So we need to train a *NER* to label this nouns as `CONCEPT`, maybe generating a custom dataset or manually checking if some nouns are concepts or no.\n\nAs an example let's see what entities are recognized in some sentences of the text","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"sample = sentences[0:10]\n\nsample_text = ' '.join([s['text'] for s in sample])\n\ndisplacy.render(nlp(sample_text), jupyter=True, style='ent')","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.204977Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.205426Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.248329Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.2054Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.247602Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<IPython.core.display.HTML object>","text/html":"<span class=\"tex2jax_ignore\"><div class=\"entities\" style=\"line-height: 2.5; direction: ltr\">\n<mark class=\"entity\" style=\"background: #7aecec; padding: 0.45em 0.6em; margin: 0 0.25em; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em;\">\n    DIGITAL SYSTEMS\n    <span style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.5rem\">ORG</span>\n</mark>\n AND INFORMATION for computations with discrete numeric elements called digits (the \n<mark class=\"entity\" style=\"background: #c887fb; padding: 0.45em 0.6em; margin: 0 0.25em; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em;\">\n    Latin\n    <span style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.5rem\">NORP</span>\n</mark>\n word for fingers)—hence the term digital computer. The use of “digital” spread from the computer to logic circuits and other systems that use discrete elements of information, giving us the terms digital circuits and digital systems. The term logic is applied to circuits that operate on a set of \n<mark class=\"entity\" style=\"background: #e4e7d2; padding: 0.45em 0.6em; margin: 0 0.25em; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em;\">\n    just two\n    <span style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.5rem\">CARDINAL</span>\n</mark>\n elements with values True (\n<mark class=\"entity\" style=\"background: #e4e7d2; padding: 0.45em 0.6em; margin: 0 0.25em; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em;\">\n    1\n    <span style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.5rem\">CARDINAL</span>\n</mark>\n) and \n<mark class=\"entity\" style=\"background: #aa9cfc; padding: 0.45em 0.6em; margin: 0 0.25em; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em;\">\n    False\n    <span style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.5rem\">PERSON</span>\n</mark>\n (0). Since computers are based on logic circuits, they operate on patterns of elements from these \n<mark class=\"entity\" style=\"background: #e4e7d2; padding: 0.45em 0.6em; margin: 0 0.25em; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em;\">\n    two\n    <span style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.5rem\">CARDINAL</span>\n</mark>\n-valued sets, which are used to represent, among other things, the decimal digits. \n<mark class=\"entity\" style=\"background: #bfe1d9; padding: 0.45em 0.6em; margin: 0 0.25em; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em;\">\n    Today\n    <span style=\"font-size: 0.8em; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1; border-radius: 0.35em; vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.5rem\">DATE</span>\n</mark>\n, the term “digital circuits” is viewed as synonymous with the term “logic circuits.” The general-purpose digital computer is a digital system that can follow a stored sequence of instructions, called a program, that operates on data. The user can specify and change the program or the data according to specific needs. As a result of this flexibility, general-purpose digital computers can perform a variety of information- processing tasks, ranging over a very wide spectrum of applications. This makes the digital computer a highly general and very flexible digital system. Also, due to its generality, complexity, and widespread use, the computer provides an ideal vehicle for learning the concepts, methods, and tools of digital system design.</div></span>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":4},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"We see that raw **NLP** can't capture concepts such as *digital circuits* or *logic circuits*, but if we look at the token level it can capture this tokens, we need a way to capture the candidates of tokens to become concepts","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(f\"Token \\t\\t\\tLemma \\t\\t\\tStopword \\tPOS\".format('Token', 'Lemma', 'Stopword', 'POS'))\nprint(\"-\"*80)\nfor sentence in sentences[3:5]:\n    sentence_tokenized = nlp(sentence['text'])\n    for token in sentence_tokenized:\n        print(f\"{str(token).ljust(10)}\\t\\t{token.lemma_.ljust(10)}\\t\\t{token.is_stop}\\t\\t{token.pos_}\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.249159Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.249465Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.271279Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.24944Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.270768Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Token \t\t\tLemma \t\t\tStopword \tPOS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSince     \t\tsince     \t\tTrue\t\tSCONJ\ncomputers \t\tcomputer  \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\nare       \t\tbe        \t\tTrue\t\tAUX\nbased     \t\tbase      \t\tFalse\t\tVERB\non        \t\ton        \t\tTrue\t\tADP\nlogic     \t\tlogic     \t\tFalse\t\tADJ\ncircuits  \t\tcircuit   \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n,         \t\t,         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\nthey      \t\tthey      \t\tTrue\t\tPRON\noperate   \t\toperate   \t\tFalse\t\tVERB\non        \t\ton        \t\tTrue\t\tADP\npatterns  \t\tpattern   \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\nof        \t\tof        \t\tTrue\t\tADP\nelements  \t\telement   \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\nfrom      \t\tfrom      \t\tTrue\t\tADP\nthese     \t\tthese     \t\tTrue\t\tDET\ntwo       \t\ttwo       \t\tTrue\t\tNUM\n-         \t\t-         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\nvalued    \t\tvalue     \t\tFalse\t\tVERB\nsets      \t\tset       \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n,         \t\t,         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\nwhich     \t\twhich     \t\tTrue\t\tPRON\nare       \t\tbe        \t\tTrue\t\tAUX\nused      \t\tuse       \t\tTrue\t\tVERB\nto        \t\tto        \t\tTrue\t\tPART\nrepresent \t\trepresent \t\tFalse\t\tVERB\n,         \t\t,         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\namong     \t\tamong     \t\tTrue\t\tADP\nother     \t\tother     \t\tTrue\t\tADJ\nthings    \t\tthing     \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n,         \t\t,         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\nthe       \t\tthe       \t\tTrue\t\tDET\ndecimal   \t\tdecimal   \t\tFalse\t\tADJ\ndigits    \t\tdigit     \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n.         \t\t.         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\nToday     \t\ttoday     \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n,         \t\t,         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\nthe       \t\tthe       \t\tTrue\t\tDET\nterm      \t\tterm      \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n“         \t\t\"         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\ndigital   \t\tdigital   \t\tFalse\t\tADJ\ncircuits  \t\tcircuit   \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n”         \t\t\"         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\nis        \t\tbe        \t\tTrue\t\tAUX\nviewed    \t\tview      \t\tFalse\t\tVERB\nas        \t\tas        \t\tTrue\t\tADP\nsynonymous\t\tsynonymous\t\tFalse\t\tADJ\nwith      \t\twith      \t\tTrue\t\tADP\nthe       \t\tthe       \t\tTrue\t\tDET\nterm      \t\tterm      \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n“         \t\t\"         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\nlogic     \t\tlogic     \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\ncircuits  \t\tcircuit   \t\tFalse\t\tNOUN\n.         \t\t.         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\n”         \t\t\"         \t\tFalse\t\tPUNCT\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"It captured *circuits* as `NOUN` and *logic* both as `NOUN` and `ADJ` in differente tokens. Based on this, we try to filter tokens that are `NOUN`,`PROPN` and `ADJ`, they aren't a Stopword and they length is greater than, say, 3.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"for sentence in sentences[3:5]:\n    sentence_tokenized = nlp(sentence['text'])\n    for token in sentence_tokenized:\n        if (token.pos_ in ['NOUN','PROPN','ADJ'] and not token.is_stop and len(token.lemma_) > 3):\n                print(token.lemma_)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.27203Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.272358Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.293626Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.272336Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.292709Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"computer\nlogic\ncircuit\npattern\nelement\nthing\ndecimal\ndigit\ntoday\nterm\ndigital\ncircuit\nsynonymous\nterm\nlogic\ncircuit\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":6},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"It's seeing a lot better for our candidates, but some of them are repetead and some concepts are span tokens such as *logic circuit* and *digital circuit*, we will use noun chunks to capture them","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"for sentence in sentences[3:5]:\n    sentence_tokenized = nlp(sentence['text'])\n    for chunk in sentence_tokenized.noun_chunks:\n        print(chunk.lemma_)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.295706Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.296262Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.320229Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.296238Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.319626Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"computer\nlogic circuit\nthey\npattern\nelement\nthese two-value set\nwhich\nother thing\nthe decimal digit\nthe term\n\"digital circuit\nthe term \"logic circuit\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":7},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Much better, we can capture *logic circuit* and *digital circuit*, let's define a cleaning function for noun chunks based on what we now know. To filter duplicates, we simply use a set to catch plurals and, as shown before, generic terms such as *thing*, *term*, *kind*, etc.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import re\n\nGENERIC_TERMS = {'think', 'term', 'way', 'type', 'kind', 'part', 'example'}\n\ndef clean_chunk(chunk):\n    lemma = chunk.lemma_.lower()\n    lemma = re.sub(r'^(the|a|an|this|these|those|which|they)\\s+', '', lemma)\n    lemma = lemma.replace('\"','').strip()\n    return lemma\n\ndef is_valid_chunk(chunk):\n    lemma = clean_chunk(chunk)\n    if len(lemma) < 4: # Drop nouns with less than 4 characters\n        return False\n    if chunk.root.pos_ == 'PRON': # Drop if they come from a pronoun\n        return False\n    if any(generic in lemma.split() for generic in GENERIC_TERMS):\n        return False\n    return True","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.321082Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.321378Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.326405Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.321356Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.325824Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":8},{"cell_type":"code","source":"for sentence in sentences[0:10]:\n    sentence_tokenized = nlp(sentence['text'])\n    for chunk in sentence_tokenized.noun_chunks:\n        if is_valid_chunk(chunk):\n            print(clean_chunk(chunk))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.327308Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.327577Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.408231Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.327556Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.407491Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"digital systems\ninformation\ncomputation\ndiscrete numeric element\ndigit\nlatin word\nfingers)—hence\ndigital computer\ndigital spread\ncomputer\nlogic circuit\nother system\ndiscrete element\ninformation\ndigital circuit\ndigital system\ncircuit\njust two element\nvalue\ncomputer\nlogic circuit\npattern\nelement\ntwo-value set\nother thing\ndecimal digit\ndigital circuit\ngeneral-purpose digital computer\ndigital system\nstore sequence\ninstruction\nprogram\ndatum\nuser\nprogram\ndatum\nspecific need\nresult\nflexibility\ngeneral-purpose digital computer\nvariety\ninformation- processing task\nvery wide spectrum\napplication\ndigital computer\nits generality\ncomplexity\nwidespread use\ncomputer\nideal vehicle\nconcept\nmethod\ntool\ndigital system design\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":9},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Pipeline","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"There are some issues still, but let's create a pipeline to run the full chapter and map the duplicates, then we choose the top candidate concepts that appear, for that we will count they appearances.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def run_pipeline_concepts(sentences):\n    texts = [s['text'] for s in sentences]\n    docs = list(nlp.pipe(texts, batch_size=32))\n    \n    concept_map = {}\n    \n    for sentence, doc in zip(sentences, docs):\n        for chunk in doc.noun_chunks:\n            if is_valid_chunk(chunk):\n                concept = clean_chunk(chunk)\n                if concept not in concept_map:\n                    concept_map[concept] = {'pages': [], 'count': 0}\n                concept_map[concept]['pages'].append(sentence['page'])\n                concept_map[concept]['count'] += 1\n\n    return concept_map\n    \n\ndef print_top_k_concepts(concept_map, k):\n    sorted_concepts = sorted(concept_map.items(), key=lambda x: x[1]['count'], reverse=True)\n    print(f'Unique concept found: {len(concept_map)}')\n    print(f'\\nTop {k} concepts:')\n    for concept, data in sorted_concepts[:k]:\n        print(f\" {concept:<20} count: {data['count']} pages: {set(data['pages'])}\")\n\ncm = run_pipeline_concepts(sentences)\nprint_top_k_concepts(cm, 20)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.409042Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.4094Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:42.091618Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:40.409375Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:42.090869Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Unique concept found: 1676\n\nTop 20 concepts:\n number