ctal and Hexadecimal Numbers` actually represents two distinct semantic concepts: `Octal` and `Hexadecimal`.\n\nThey are a great source and alternative we could dive more in the future to work with other strategies.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Relationships\n\nFor capturing relationships we will use two techinques: \n- **bootstrapping** using our concepts as seeds to automatially capture the most frequent relationship betweent them are\n- **Dependency Parsing** capture the relations based on what we see in the text\n\nThey could complement each other","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Bootstrapping\n\nThe general idea of bootstrapping is like a `GREP`, we match the strings that have our concepts, then we see what's between them, relationships will emerge as more common they are.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from collections import Counter\nimport re\n\ndef get_text_between(sentence, concept_a, concept_b):\n    pattern = rf'{re.escape(concept_a)}(.+?){re.escape(concept_b)}'\n    match = re.search(pattern, sentence.lower())\n    if match:\n        return match.group(1).strip()\n    return None\n\ndef bootstrap_relations(sentence, concept_map, top_k=20, min_count=2):\n    top_concepts = [c for c, _ in sorted(\n        concept_map.items(),\n        key=lambda x: x[1]['count'],\n        reverse=True\n    )[:top_k]]\n\n    between_patterns = Counter()\n    relation_examples = {}\n\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        text = sentence['text'].lower()\n\n        for i, concept_a in enumerate(top_concepts):\n            for concept_b in top_concepts[i+1:]:\n                if concept_a not in text or concept_b not in text:\n                    continue\n\n                between = get_text_between(text, concept_a, concept_b)\n                if not between:\n                    between = get_text_between(text, concept_b, concept_a)\n                    if between:\n                        concept_a, concept_b = concept_b, concept_a\n\n                if between and 2 < len(between.split()) < 4:\n                    between_patterns[between] += 1\n\n                    if between not in relation_examples:\n                        relation_examples[between] = []\n                    if len(relation_examples[between]) < 3:\n                        relation_examples[between].append(f'({concept_a}) [{between}] ({concept_b})')\n\n    print('Most frequent patterns between concepts:\\n')\n    for pattern, count in between_patterns.most_common(20):\n        if count >= min_count:\n            print(f\" '{pattern}' -> count: {count}\")\n            for ex in relation_examples[pattern]:\n                print(f\"    e.g. {ex}\")\n            print()\n            \n    return between_patterns, relation_examples","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.525524Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.525835Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.540681Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.525811Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.539916Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":19},{"cell_type":"code","source":"patterns, examples = bootstrap_relations(sentences, concepts_nc, top_k=50, min_count=2)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.541546Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.542334Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.672532Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.54231Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-04T05:55:59.671791Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Most frequent patterns between concepts:\n\n 's and in' -> count: 21\n    e.g. (digital system) [s and in] (form)\n    e.g. (digital system) [s and in] (form)\n    e.g. (digital system) [s and in] (form)\n\n 's of the' -> count: 5\n    e.g. (coefficient) [s of the] (binary number)\n    e.g. (coefficient) [s of the] (binary)\n    e.g. (coefficient) [s of the] (binary number)\n\n 's for the' -